  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tackling Maternal and Child Undernutrition in Zambia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To improve national nutrition response focused on addressing direct and underlying causes of stunting among children under 5 yearsTo improve child nutrition by providing children under 5 with direct nutrition support (Vitamin A and deworming tablets), piloting improved access to anti-diarrhoea kits, testing the efficacy of vitamin A enriched maize and supporting the government of Zambia to scale up nutrition programmes.  This will benefit 200,000 children and reduce child undernutrition. This contributes towards our MDG 1 and will result in at least 100,000 less Zambian children being stunted by 2015</narrative>
  </description>
